 `prob_grid_fit` (`yes|no`, default `no`) is a developer key pending promotion.
 In the multi-state probabilistic table it replaces the L-BFGS-B alternations of
-every refined reference by a quadratic fit to the coarse shift grid, where the
-grid minimum has a full 3 x 3 stencil, the fitted curvature is positive definite
-and well conditioned, the step stays inside the centre cell and the search box,
-and one exact evaluation at the fitted shift beats the grid minimum. Otherwise
-the alternations run from the grid minimum as before. The bench file counts the
-fits kept and the fallbacks per reason. The key is read by `fill_tab_range` and
+every refined reference by a quadratic fit to the coarse shift grid: a 3 x 3
+stencil centred on the grid minimum, or one lattice point inside when the grid
+minimum is on the edge of the 5 x 5 lattice, so that it always contains the
+minimum. The fit is kept where the fitted curvature is positive definite and
+well conditioned, the fitted shift lies within half a grid step of the grid
+minimum and inside the search box, and one exact evaluation at the fitted shift
+beats the grid minimum. Otherwise the alternations run from the grid minimum as
+before. The bench file counts the fits kept (and how many of them used an
+edge-centred stencil) and the fallbacks per reason. The key is read by `fill_tab_range` and
 reaches `prob_tab` through the `prob_align` command line.
 
 `prob_grid_ptcl` and `prob_seed_ptcl` (`yes|no`, default `no`) are developer
